Package: SPASAM.MSE
Title: Spatially Explicit Management Strategy Evaluation for WHAM-Based Stock Assessments
Type: Package
Version: 0.1.0
Author: Chengxue Li <chengxue.li@noaa.gov>
Maintainer: Chengxue Li <chengxue.li@noaa.gov>
Description: A flexible and extensible framework for conducting spatially explicit
    Management Strategy Evaluation (MSE) for marine fish stocks using the Woods Hole
    Assessment Model (WHAM). SPASAM-MSE provides a fully configurable multi-stock,
    multi-region operating model that supports complex spatial population structure,
    including natal homing, source???sink dynamics, and bidirectional or unidirectional
    movement. Movement processes can be specified as fixed or random effects and may
    vary by age, year, stock, season, and region, with optional environmental covariate
    effects.
    
    The package enables closed-loop MSE by integrating operating models, data
    generation (fishery-dependent and fishery-independent), alternative estimation
    models, projections, harvest control rules, and management implementation error.
    Tools are provided to evaluate assessment bias, uncertainty, and management
    performance metrics (e.g., catch, spawning biomass, fishing mortality, overfishing
    risk) across space, time, and simulation replicates.
    
    SPASAM-MSE includes a comprehensive plotting and reporting pipeline for
    large-scale simulation experiments, supporting automated generation of PNG, PDF,
    and HTML outputs. A Shiny-based graphical interface is included to facilitate
    interactive configuration of biological parameters, fisheries structure, and
    movement models for reproducible spatial MSE experiments.
